  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "All public device/child state model types (e.g. LightState, FanState, ChildBatterySensorState, ChildContactSensorState, ChildLockState, and similar snapshot types in Models.cs) are now declared as sealed records instead of sealed classes, giving them value-based Equals/GetHashCode/==/!= and a descriptive ToString() instead of default reference identity. This is useful because most of these state snapshots are recomputed on every property access rather than cached, so consumers comparing two reads for changes previously always saw them as unequal even when nothing changed. No properties, constructors, or public API signatures changed; this is a source- and binary-compatible change for all reasonable existing usage.",
